[
  "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The scene features two matte ceramic bowls centered in the frame, one in clear focus and the second slightly blurred in the background, showcasing the Creamy Dijon Mushroom and Lentil dish. The camera is positioned at a 3/4 overhead angle, ensuring every component is visible while maintaining a shallow depth of field. The scene is illuminated by soft, natural side light from a window on the left, casting gentle, natural shadows across a rustic, aged oak wood table with visible grain and small, authentic use marks. To the side of the bowls, a worn linen napkin is rumpled naturally, with a few stray fresh thyme leaves and a small pinch of chopped walnuts scattered on the wood surface near the bowls. The farro serves as a warm, chewy base in each bowl, topped with a generous portion of deeply browned, caramelized cremini mushrooms and brown lentils coated in a rich, velvety, pale-creamy Dijon yogurt sauce. The mushrooms display realistic golden-brown edges and a glistening sheen from the olive oil. A scattering of chopped walnuts provides textural contrast on top. There is a small, natural sauce drip on the rim of the foreground bowl. The composition feels lived-in, warm, and authentic, as if just finished in a home kitchen. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. Warm, golden-hour color temperature, cozy and inviting. No plastic sheen, no unnaturally smooth surfaces, no perfect symmetry. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. The image should be indistinguishable from a photograph taken by a professional food photographer for a printed cookbook."
]
